">>> jaws = Movie('Jaws')\n"
">>> f'Released in {jaws.year} by {jaws.director}'\n"
"'Released in 1975 by Steven Spielberg'\n"
"\n"
">>> Song('Country Roads').artist\n"
"'John Denver'\n"
"\n"
">>> Movie('Star Wars').director = 'J.J. Abrams'\n"
">>> Movie('Star Wars').director\n"
"'J.J. Abrams'"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:952
msgid "Pure Python Equivalents"
msgstr "Reine Python-Gegenstücke"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:954
msgid ""
"The descriptor protocol is simple and offers exciting possibilities.  "
"Several use cases are so common that they have been prepackaged into built-"
"in tools. Properties, bound methods, static methods, class methods, and "
"\\_\\_slots\\_\\_ are all based on the descriptor protocol."
msgstr ""
"Das Deskriptor-Protokoll ist einfach und bietet spannende Möglichkeiten. "
"Mehrere Anwendungsfälle sind so verbreitet, dass sie in integrierten "
"Werkzeugen fertig verpackt sind. Properties, gebundene Methoden, statische "
"Methoden, Klassenmethoden und \\_\\_slots\\_\\_ beruhen alle auf dem "
"Deskriptor-Protokoll."

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:961
msgid "Properties"
msgstr "Properties"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:963
msgid ""
"Calling :func:`property` is a succinct way of building a data descriptor "
"that triggers a function call upon access to an attribute.  Its signature "
"is::"
msgstr ""
":func:`property` aufzurufen ist ein knapper Weg, einen Datendeskriptor zu "
"bauen, der beim Zugriff auf ein Attribut einen Funktionsaufruf auslöst. "
"Seine Signatur ist::"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:966
msgid "property(fget=None, fset=None, fdel=None, doc=None) -> property"
msgstr "property(fget=None, fset=None, fdel=None, doc=None) -> property"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:968
msgid ""
"The documentation shows a typical use to define a managed attribute ``x``:"
msgstr ""
"Die Dokumentation zeigt eine typische Verwendung, um ein verwaltetes "
"Attribut ``x`` zu definieren:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:970
msgid ""
"class C:\n"
"    def getx(self): return self.__x\n"
"    def setx(self, value): self.__x = value\n"
"    def delx(self): del self.__x\n"
"    x = property(getx, setx, delx, \"I'm the 'x' property.\")"
msgstr ""
"class C:\n"
"    def getx(self): return self.__x\n"
"    def setx(self, value): self.__x = value\n"
"    def delx(self): del self.__x\n"
"    x = property(getx, setx, delx, \"I'm the 'x' property.\")"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:992
msgid ""
"To see how :func:`property` is implemented in terms of the descriptor "
"protocol, here is a pure Python equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:995
msgid ""
"class Property:\n"
"    \"Emulate PyProperty_Type() in Objects/descrobject.c\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, fget=None, fset=None, fdel=None, doc=None):\n"
"        self.fget = fget\n"
"        self.fset = fset\n"
"        self.fdel = fdel\n"
"        if doc is None and fget is not None:\n"
"            doc = fget.__doc__\n"
"        self.__doc__ = doc\n"
"        self._name = ''\n"
"\n"
"    def __set_name__(self, owner, name):\n"
"        self._name = name\n"
"\n"
"    def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):\n"
"        if obj is None:\n"
"            return self\n"
"        if self.fget is None:\n"
"            raise AttributeError(\n"
"                f'property {self._name!r} of {type(obj).__name__!r} object "
"has no getter'\n"
"             )\n"
"        return self.fget(obj)\n"
"\n"
"    def __set__(self, obj, value):\n"
"        if self.fset is None:\n"
"            raise AttributeError(\n"
"                f'property {self._name!r} of {type(obj).__name__!r} object "
"has no setter'\n"
"             )\n"
"        self.fset(obj, value)\n"
"\n"
"    def __delete__(self, obj):\n"
"        if self.fdel is None:\n"
"            raise AttributeError(\n"
"                f'property {self._name!r} of {type(obj).__name__!r} object "
"has no deleter'\n"
"             )\n"
"        self.fdel(obj)\n"
"\n"
"    def getter(self, fget):\n"
"        prop = type(self)(fget, self.fset, self.fdel, self.__doc__)\n"
"        prop._name = self._name\n"
"        return prop\n"
"\n"
"    def setter(self, fset):\n"
"        prop = type(self)(self.fget, fset, self.fdel, self.__doc__)\n"
"        prop._name = self._name\n"
"        return prop\n"
"\n"
"    def deleter(self, fdel):\n"
"        prop = type(self)(self.fget, self.fset, fdel, self.__doc__)\n"
"        prop._name = self._name\n"
"        return prop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1132
msgid ""
"The :func:`property` builtin helps whenever a user interface has granted "
"attribute access and then subsequent changes require the intervention of a "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Die integrierte Funktion :func:`property` hilft immer dann, wenn eine "
"Benutzeroberfläche Attributzugriff gewährt hat und spätere Änderungen das "
"Eingreifen einer Methode erfordern."

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1136
msgid ""
"For instance, a spreadsheet class may grant access to a cell value through "
"``Cell('b10').value``. Subsequent improvements to the program require the "
"cell to be recalculated on every access; however, the programmer does not "
"want to affect existing client code accessing the attribute directly.  The "
"solution is to wrap access to the value attribute in a property data "
"descriptor:"
msgstr ""
"So kann eine Tabellenkalkulationsklasse zum Beispiel über "
"``Cell('b10').value`` Zugriff auf einen Zellenwert gewähren. Spätere "
"Verbesserungen am Programm erfordern, dass die Zelle bei jedem Zugriff neu "
"berechnet wird. Der Programmierer will bestehenden Clientcode, der "
"unmittelbar auf das Attribut zugreift, aber nicht beeinträchtigen. Die "
"Lösung ist, den Zugriff auf das Attribut value in einen property-"
"Datendeskriptor zu hüllen:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1142
msgid ""
"class Cell:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"    @property\n"
"    def value(self):\n"
"        \"Recalculate the cell before returning value\"\n"
"        self.recalc()\n"
"        return self._value"
msgstr ""
"class Cell:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"    @property\n"
"    def value(self):\n"
"        \"Recalculate the cell before returning value\"\n"
"        self.recalc()\n"
"        return self._value"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1153
msgid ""
"Either the built-in :func:`property` or our :func:`!Property` equivalent "
"would work in this example."
msgstr ""
"In diesem Beispiel würden sowohl die integrierte Funktion :func:`property` "
"als auch unser Gegenstück :func:`!Property` funktionieren."

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1158
msgid "Functions and methods"
msgstr "Funktionen und Methoden"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1160
msgid ""
"Python's object oriented features are built upon a function based "
"environment. Using non-data descriptors, the two are merged seamlessly."
msgstr ""
"Die objektorientierten Eigenschaften von Python ruhen auf einer "
"funktionsbasierten Umgebung. Über Nicht-Datendeskriptoren werden die beiden "
"bruchlos verbunden."

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1163
msgid ""
"Functions stored in class dictionaries get turned into methods when invoked. "
"Methods only differ from regular functions in that the object instance is "
"prepended to the other arguments.  By convention, the instance is called "
"*self* but could be called *this* or any other variable name."
msgstr ""
"In Klassenwörterbüchern abgelegte Funktionen werden beim Aufruf zu Methoden. "
"Methoden unterscheiden sich von gewöhnlichen Funktionen nur darin, dass die "
"Objektinstanz den anderen Argumenten vorangestellt wird. Per Konvention "
"heißt die Instanz *self*, könnte aber *this* oder wie jede andere Variable "
"heißen."

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1168
msgid ""
"Methods can be created manually with :class:`types.MethodType` which is "
"roughly equivalent to:"
msgstr ""
"Methoden lassen sich mit :class:`types.MethodType` von Hand erzeugen, was "
"etwa Folgendem entspricht:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1171
msgid ""
"class MethodType:\n"
"    \"Emulate PyMethod_Type in Objects/classobject.c\"\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, func, obj):\n"
"        self.__func__ = func\n"
"        self.__self__ = obj\n"
"\n"
"    def __call__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n"
"        func = self.__func__\n"
"        obj = self.__self__\n"
"        return func(obj, *args, **kwargs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1185
msgid ""
"To support automatic creation of methods, functions include "
"the :meth:`~object.__get__` method for binding methods during attribute "
"access.  This means that functions are non-data descriptors that return "
"bound methods during dotted lookup from an instance.  Here's how it works:"
msgstr ""
"Um die automatische Erzeugung von Methoden zu unterstützen, haben Funktionen "
"die Methode :meth:`~object.__get__`, um Methoden beim Attributzugriff zu "
"binden. Das heißt, dass Funktionen Nicht-Datendeskriptoren sind, die beim "
"Nachschlagen mit Punkt aus einer Instanz gebundene Methoden zurückgeben. So "
"funktioniert es:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1190
msgid ""
"class Function:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"    def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):\n"
"        \"Simulate func_descr_get() in Objects/funcobject.c\"\n"
"        if obj is None:\n"
"            return self\n"
"        return MethodType(self, obj)"
msgstr ""
"class Function:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"    def __get__(self, obj, objtype=None):\n"
"        \"Simulate func_descr_get() in Objects/funcobject.c\"\n"
"        if obj is None:\n"
"            return self\n"
"        return MethodType(self, obj)"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1201
msgid ""
"Running the following class in the interpreter shows how the function "
"descriptor works in practice:"
msgstr ""
"Lässt man die folgende Klasse im Interpreter laufen, zeigt sich, wie der "
"Funktionsdeskriptor in der Praxis arbeitet:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1204
msgid ""
"class D:\n"
"    def f(self, x):\n"
"         return x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1210
msgid ""
"The function has a :term:`qualified name` attribute to support introspection:"
msgstr ""
"Die Funktion hat ein Attribut :term:`qualifizierter Name <qualified name>`, "
"um Introspektion zu unterstützen:"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1212
msgid ""
">>> D.f.__qualname__\n"
"'D.f'"
msgstr ""
">>> D.f.__qualname__\n"
"'D.f'"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1217
msgid ""
"Accessing the function through the class dictionary does not "
"invoke :meth:`~object.__get__`.  Instead, it just returns the underlying "
"function object::"
msgstr ""
"Auf die Funktion über das Klassenwörterbuch zuzugreifen "
"ruft :meth:`~object.__get__` nicht auf. Es gibt stattdessen einfach das "
"darunterliegende Funktionsobjekt zurück::"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1220
msgid ""
">>> D.__dict__['f']\n"
"<function D.f at 0x00C45070>"
msgstr ""
">>> D.__dict__['f']\n"
"<function D.f at 0x00C45070>"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1223
msgid ""
"Dotted access from a class calls :meth:`~object.__get__` which just returns "
"the underlying function unchanged::"
msgstr ""
"Der Zugriff mit Punkt aus einer Klasse ruft :meth:`~object.__get__` auf, das "
"die darunterliegende Funktion einfach unverändert zurückgibt::"

#: ../../howto/descriptor.rst:1226
